\pard\b\f0\fs24 Tao Vang\b0\f1\fs18\par
\b\f0\par
Ethnicity:\b0\f1  Not clearly stated in manuscript.\par
\b\f0 Position:\b0\f1  Lieutenant, engineer and team tech.\par
\b\f0 Age:\b0\f1  32.\par
\b\f0 Sex:\b0\f1  Female.\par
\b\f0 Height:\b0\f1  Not stated.\par
\b\f0 Build:\b0\f1  Not stated.\par
\b\f0 Role in Story:\b0\f1  John's technical backbone. Tao keeps the squad's suits, weapons, sensors and ships operational and is usually the first person solving a systems failure under pressure.\par
\b\f0 Goal:\b0\f1  Keep the team alive through engineering discipline and make sense of every black-box system put in front of her.\par
\b\f0 Physical Description:\b0\f1  Carries herself with clean precision and confident posture. Her expression hardens quickly when she does not trust a system.\par
\b\f0 Personality:\b0\f1  Analytical, skeptical, disciplined and dryly funny. She is confident in her engineering judgment and protective of the people who depend on it.\par
\b\f0 Occupation:\b0\f1  Protectant engineer and field systems specialist.\par
\b\f0 Habits/Mannerisms:\b0\f1  Takes notes constantly. Answers technical questions directly. Pushes back on unsafe assumptions even when John is briefing the room.\par
\b\f0 Background:\b0\f1  Based on Ceres and integrated into John's squad as its resident engineer. She handles hacking, suit logic, sensor interpretation and rail-weapon systems.\par
\b\f0 Internal Conflicts:\b0\f1  She wants to trust progress, but she mistrusts any technology whose limits have not been honestly explained.\par
\b\f0 External Conflicts:\b0\f1  Marcellus's secrecy repeatedly forces her to work blind, from the lost facility to the Europa operations.\par
\b\f0 Notes:\b0\f1  The manuscript alternates between "Tao" and "Tau"; both clearly refer to the same character.\par
